Praised for the luminous warmth of her voice and the dramatic truth of her portrayals, **Anna Avdalyan** is one of the most compelling sopranos of her generation. Her repertoire spans the lyric heroines of Mozart and Puccini to the great dramatic roles of Verdi, and she is equally at home on the opera stage, in the concert hall and in the intimacy of the song recital.

Recent and upcoming highlights include Violetta in *La traviata*, Mimì in *La bohème* and the Contessa in *Le nozze di Figaro*, as well as Brahms' *Ein deutsches Requiem* and Strauss' *Vier letzte Lieder* with leading European orchestras. In the coming season she prepares the title role of Dvořák's *Rusalka*.

Anna Avdalyan studied voice and opera performance and refined her art in masterclasses with renowned singers. She is a prize-winner of several international singing competitions. For engagements, please visit the [contact page](/contact).
